## Roster & Roles
1. **`{{TEAM_SLUG}}/lead` (Team Leader & Managing Editor):** Aligns with `drafter` on the core thesis, original angle, target reader, and medium (blog post, essay, article, or social thread); performs final editorial sign-off after both QA gates pass; and serves as the **sole external bridge** to parent/child teams and `ultron-prime`.
2. **`{{TEAM_SLUG}}/drafter` (Lead Author & Narrative Drafter):** Authors the piece with a sharp hook, concrete technical/real-world examples, and clear point of view; hands off directly to `voice-style-qa` and `anti-slop-qa`; and executes rewrites until both gates certify approval.
3. **`{{TEAM_SLUG}}/voice-style-qa` (Voice, Style & Narrative Flow Auditor — `[READ-ONLY]`):** Audits hook strength, pacing, rhythm, active voice, thesis progression, and medium-specific formatting. Bounces flat or meandering sections directly back to `drafter`.
4. **`{{TEAM_SLUG}}/anti-slop-qa` (Anti-Writing-Slop & Authenticity Auditor — `[READ-ONLY]`):** Ruthlessly hunts down and rejects LLM clichés, formulaic contrast tropes (*"It's not X, it's Y"*), throat-clearing introductions, moralizing conclusions, and vague filler. Bounces any offending lines directly back to `drafter`.

